  - urban heat
  - covered walkways
  - openstreetmap
  - maplibre
  - makati
  - metro manila
  - civic technology
abstract: >
  undercover.ph finds walking routes in 13 areas of Metro Manila that stay in shade on sunny
  days or under cover when it rains, a Philippine take on Singapore's
  Undercover prototype. It casts shadows from OpenStreetMap and Google Open
  Buildings heights and from a tree canopy height raster, every 30 minutes for
  each sidewalk edge, and routes in the browser with a custom A* search that
  returns the shortest, the most covered, and a recommended route. Paths with
  unchecked access, closed mall passages, and mid-block road crossings stay out
  of routes. The shade values are modelled and not yet checked in the field.
